<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Ukrainian People's Republic of Soviets</h1><p class="st-meta">1917 CE – 1918 CE · capital Kharkiv</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The first Soviet government in Ukraine, set up by Bolsheviks in Kharkiv as a rival to the Central Rada in Kiev.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In December 1917, after Bolshevik delegates walked out of a congress of soviets in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> dominated by supporters of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-rada">Central Rada</a>, they held their own congress in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharkiv">Kharkiv</a>. It proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> a republic of soviets in federation with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>, in opposition to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ukrainian-peoples-republic">Ukrainian People's Republic</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government, called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-secretariat">People's Secretariat</a>, included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yevgenia-bosch">Yevhenia Bosh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mykola-skrypnyk">Mykola Skrypnyk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volodymyr-zatonsky">Volodymyr Zatonsky</a>. It depended heavily on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-russia">Red Guards</a> sent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, which under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-artemyevich-muravyov">Mikhail Muravyov</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> in February 1918 and carried out mass killings there. Its authority was weak, and several other Soviet republics existed alongside it in eastern and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>, German and Austro-Hungarian troops drove the Bolsheviks out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. In March 1918 the republic merged with the other Soviet republics into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukrainian-soviet-republic">Ukrainian Soviet Republic</a>, which was dissolved in April as its leaders withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets.jpg" alt="Ukrainian People's Republic of Soviets" width="320" height="209"><figcaption>Image: I Gauravjuvekar vectorized the above file. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ukrainian_People%27s_Republic_of_the_Soviets.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1917 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kharkiv</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yevhenia Bosh, Mykola Skrypnyk, Volodymyr Zatonsky</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>State atheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Ukrainian, Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ukraine">Ukraine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Soviet Ukraine (1917-1918)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets" aria-label="Ukrainian People's Republic of Soviets on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5510 438 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ukrainian People's Republic of Soviets lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5830 694L5820 533M5830 694L5697 681M5830 694L5830 694"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M5697 681h0M5830 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5830 694h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5830 694h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kharkiv. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=ukrainian-peoples-republic-of-soviets">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
